# Voxy Vulkan integration direction

Owner decision, 2026-10-04: complete Voxy on Minecraft's own Vulkan backend
(`Prefer Vulkan`), using MoltenVK on macOS. Read `docs/ai/project-goal.md` before
planning Vulkan work; it defines scope, priority and acceptance evidence.

- New Vulkan integration must not require a GL context, GL texture IDs/casts,
  or IOSurface/CGL-to-GL composition. Do not expand/productize the GL diagnostic
  route as the next milestone or introduce a GL fallback requirement.
- Reuse shared CPU/model/meshing and Vulkan rendering logic. Preserve the existing
  OpenGL backend, shared shaders and historical evidence; do not delete GL code
  just because the Vulkan target is changing its integration route.
- Prioritize a minimal draw connected to Minecraft's Vulkan device, color/depth
  targets and submission/resource lifetimes before expanding diagnostic features.
- Verify the actual Minecraft backend. A Voxy Vulkan enum, preference setting,
  offscreen pass or GL-hosted live pass does not prove native integration.
- Keep implemented state and intended architecture distinct. Follow `AGENTS.md`
  and `docs/ai/constraints.md` for the remaining repository rules.
